# tools/check-hostptr.py: findings that are right. path<TAB>text<TAB>reason
# (the text a fragment of the finding's line, whitespace collapsed)
crates/ffx-host/src/d3d11.rs	OutputWindow: HWND(w[11] as usize as *mut _),	a window handle, not an address: the real window CreateWindowExA forwarded (win_forward.rs), whose value fits 32 bits as every HWND does
crates/ffx-host/src/exec.rs	uc_emu_stop(h as *mut std::ffi::c_void);	Unicorn's own instance handle (a host pointer kept as usize in Shared::emulators), never a game address
crates/ffx-host/src/tcg_commit.rs	at as *const _,	a host address: the faulting address of Unicorn's translation buffer from the exception record (Windows, host memory), queried and committed (VirtualQuery, VirtualAlloc)
crates/ffx-movie/src/api.rs	u32::try_from(p as usize).unwrap_or(0)	addr(): the hook's paths only (vpx_get_frame, vorbis_pcmout, called by ported/movie.rs under cfg(not(ffx_host))); ffx-host calls vpx_get_frame_in_game / vorbis_pcmout_in_game, which copy into the game's malloc
crates/ffx-movie/src/mkv.rs	u32::try_from(p as usize).unwrap_or(0)	addr(): a segment without a game block (create_instance, ported/movie.rs under cfg(not(ffx_host))); ffx-host's create_instance_at sets Segment::game, so base() and the codec private data use the arena block
